Melee-NX-NetPlay: Training Mode CE's memory card operations finish (the Lab's Export, the Lab character select's Import).
TM-CE waits in Memcard_Wait until its card callback sets MemcardWork.is_done. Two things kept that from ever happening
natively, and the game froze on the Export screen:
- TM-CE's MemcardWork (MexTK memcard.h) is the console's layout of the game's card block, where is_done (0x8ac) is the
  game's task counter; natively that block (lbcardnew.c state) has another layout, and the callback TM-CE named
  (mu_tmce_fn_onCardComplete) decremented the game's own counter. TM-CE now has a block of its own and a callback that
  sets its is_done (tmce/native/tmce_runtime.c, mextk_redefine.txt); the game's card state is no longer touched;
- the card's completion is a queued event natively (shim/mu_card.c mu_post), not an interrupt arriving during the loop:
  the wait delivers the queued events.
Only TM-CE's code changes (the reference scripts never run it).
